### API #64 — Update Question

| Item | Value |
|------|-------|
| **Method** | `PUT` |
| **URL** | `/api/college/update_question/:questionId` |
| **Auth** | Bearer Token (COLLEGEADMIN or TPO) |

#### Request Body (at least 1 field required)

```json
{
  "question_text": "Which city do you prefer for posting?",
  "question_options": ["Mumbai", "Delhi", "Pune", "Bangalore"],
  "question_order": 2
}
```

All fields optional but min 1 required. Additional field `question_order` (1–100) can be used for reordering.

> [!WARNING]
> **Cannot edit questions if the published job already has student applications.** The API blocks this to prevent data inconsistency.
> If you need to modify questions after applications exist, close the job first.

#### Special Type-Change Rules
- Changing **non-MCQ → MCQ**: `question_options` is **required** in the same request
- Changing **MCQ → non-MCQ**: `question_options` is **auto-cleared** (set to null)
- Changing MCQ options: provide the full new options array

---

### API #65 — Delete Question

| Item | Value |
|------|-------|
| **Method** | `DELETE` |
| **URL** | `/api/college/delete_question/:questionId` |
| **Auth** | Bearer Token (COLLEGEADMIN or TPO) |

No request body needed. This is a **hard delete** — the question is permanently removed. Remaining questions are **auto-reordered** to maintain sequential `question_order`.

#### Success Response (200)

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Record deleted successfully",
  "data": {
    "question_id": "...",
    "question_text": "Are you willing to relocate?",
    "job_id": "...",
    "job_title": "Software Developer",
    "company_name": "TCS",
    "deleted": true
  }
}
```

